    },
    "body": "The accepted raw-text Python reader/core/R4 path lacked a defined native artifact and consumer contract. This change specifies `R4LearnedReferenceV1`: an opt-in Rust research reference with one raw-byte four-fact operation, an exact 21-component artifact, trusted loader/admission rules, unchanged codec/result semantics, and a fixed scalar f32/f64 operator profile.\n\nIt separately freezes the minimum future Python/native comparison on the original 320 authoring rows and 16 refusals, including exact discrete criteria, all four complete tensors, a new per-row/per-tensor 1e-5 absolute ceiling, replay, full evidence retention and explicit load/time/RSS/byte budgets. Native preservation remains unproven. No implementation, artifact export, model load/forward, fit, comparison, replay or withheld access ran.\n\nThe original-source and operator audits inspect relevant NEMESIS/W33/UOR research and accepted code without importing proof or capability claims. Independent specification review accepted the contract after resolving loader mutation reachability, trusted field equality, reference failure classification and gate load accounting. The current roadmap, continuation prompt and claim ledger preserve prior measured, negative, unavailable and descriptive records. #1102 is the parked, unassigned implementation/export/comparison successor.\n\nValidation: independent specification and operator reviews; 55 focused source/metadata/shape/identity/accounting checks; claim-wording and diff-whitespace checks. Broad QA is dormant; required GitHub checks are repository transport acknowledgements. Storage was reviewed without deleting evidence or user material.\n\nReferences #1086. Close the specification manually only after verifying protected delivery. #973 remains open and #954 blocked; #1083/#1087 retain their separate integration/lowering scope.\n",
